{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H01 — Inventory selector: add an explicit selection policy\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Localized API evolution (1/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic inventory-selector program.\nIts selection API, given a list of items and a minimum quantity, picks the\neligible item (quantity >= minimum) with the **highest priority**; ties are\nbroken deterministically by insertion order. Two call sites in the same module\nuse that API (one returns the picked item, one reports its id).\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H01_SCENARIO` (scenario\nname) and prints exactly one line of output per scenario. There is no\npersistence, no network, and no wall-clock dependency; everything is\ndeterministic.\n\n## Required change\n\nExtend the selection API with an explicit **policy** parameter so callers can\nchoose how a selection is made:\n\n1. `policy = \"priority\"` — the existing behavior: eligible item with the\n   highest priority, ties broken by insertion order (earlier wins).\n2. `policy = \"qty\"` — eligible item with the **largest quantity**, ties broken\n   by insertion order.\n3. `policy = \"first\"` — the **first eligible item** in list order.\n4. Any other policy value — the operation must fail with an explicit error\n   whose text starts with `E_H01_POLICY:` and includes the offending value.\n\nEvery existing call site must accept and honor the policy parameter; none may\nkeep a silently fixed policy. Existing behavior under `policy = \"priority\"`\nmust remain unchanged (same outputs for the same inputs).\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier builds the project and drives the compiled program through\nscenarios via `H01_SCENARIO`, then checks the exact output lines. It covers:\n\n- preserved base behavior (priority selection, tie-break, no-eligible error);\n- each of the three policy modes;\n- the explicit unknown-policy error;\n- both call sites honoring a non-default policy.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
